A||||11||RiceCooker||To Those who have replaced Clutch Master Cylinder....||||5||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||04-02-2001||08:50 PM||||Did you replace the slave cylinder at the same time as the master cylinder?<P>Is there a specific NEED to?<P>Or did you choose not to and have any problems afterwards?<P>I'm 90% sure it's my master cylinder and i'm just curious if i should do both. Any input is appreciated.<P>Thanks,<BR>Todd<P>------------------<BR>Kids in the back seat cause accidents<BR>Accidents in the back seat cause kids||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wade87GT||04-02-2001||09:53 PM||||If either cylinder went bad, it was probably from some contaminants in the system. Replace the bad component (#1) and now the other is the weak link (#2). So #2 usually goes bad shortly thereafter. Now, #1 is contaminated and #2 will be also after you replace that. The circle of life. I like to think of a short term solution to achieve a long term goal. So I replaced both (using GM parts from <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/</A>  You'll save some money but will need the correct part numbers based on model and trans.). Don't forget to flush out the clutch line. I used isopropol alcohol for that. It works great, bled easily, and no mushiness or extra pedal travel. Hope this helps.<P>Wade||||reg||14
Z||000002||RiceCooker||04-03-2001||10:02 AM||||Thanks Wade||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||04-04-2001||07:51 AM||||I agree.  When one goes, the other is soon to follow.  That happened to my 85SE v-6 4spd.  The master went out one week.  I rebuilt it.  The slave went out the next week.  No rebuild kit was available so I replaced it with a re-man.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||04-04-2001||01:32 PM||||I replaced my master... broke the "ear" on the slave trying to loosen the rusted bleeder screw... had to wait 2 or 3 more days for the slave. I got both from NAPA. It's an 88 so they were pretty pricey. They are lifetime guarantee though... I figured it was worth it with all the problems we have with clutch hydraulics. I used the guarantee once already on the slave when I broke the "ear" again about a year later when I overtightened the bleeder screw.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||sparks||04-04-2001||08:28 PM||||So is it better to replace the cylinders with new units or is a rebuild kit ok??  Substantially cheaper, however if it's not worth it in the long run I'll buy new parts and totally replace what I have.<P>Right now one of my cylinders is leaking somewhere.  If you hold the clutch with it in gear long enough it engages with out you ever taking your foot off the pedal.  Still works, for now, but I'm looking to fix it soon.<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||5
Z||000006||Wade87GT||04-05-2001||09:10 AM||||I paid less for new parts at <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmpartsdirect.com/</A>  then what you'd pay at your usual parts stores. Do a search here using the keyword clutch and you'll receive 200 threads to read. Then you can decide for yourself which is best, new or used. Here's the "Clutch Thread from Hell" for starters: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000034.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/000034.html</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||04-05-2001||11:22 AM||||My .02 is to always use new GM clutch hydraulic parts.....those aftermarket ones just don't hold up as well in the long run (those broken "ears" are all too common....a design flaw with the aftermarket slaves).<P>You can get a slave for a Getrag at GMPartsDirect for around $100, which is a great price.  I believe I paid $125 for my NAPA one several years ago (wich I replace 3 times in a 6 onth period).<P>At any rate, that's my opinion and hopefully we don;t start another thread from hell on clutches!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||sparks||04-05-2001||11:42 AM||||I tried the GM PartsDirect Website but can't find any parts for Fieros.  It only seems to want to let me go back to '94 and since I don't have part #'s for MC and Slave Cyl. it's kinda hard to find 'em.  Any of you have those GM numbers?<P>I kinda figured new was the way to go anyhow...<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||5
